#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171756 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8fa39c-a982-569a-b2e0-833c51259711" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 3 or 9"}] :question/id #uuid "b926f4d4-513a-5b05-8ce2-bedc39784ada" :question/math-academy-id "e-15012" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $3$ and $9?$\n\nI. $176\\,850$\n\nII. $1\\,362\\,448$\n\nIII. $68\\,543\\,031$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$ Likewise, a number is divisible by $9$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $176\\,850$ is\n\n$$\n1+7+6+8+5+0 = 27,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by both $3$ and $9.$ So, $176\\,850$ is divisible by both $3$ and $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $1\\,362\\,448$ is\n\n$$\n1+3+6+2+4+4+8 = 28,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $3.$ So, $1\\,362\\,448$ is *not* divisible by $3.$ Also, since it is not divisible by $3,$ it cannot be divisible by $9$ either.\n\n- The sum of the digits of $68\\,543\\,031$ is\n\n$$\n6+8+5+4+3+0+3+1 = 30,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3,$ but not divisible $9.$ So, $68\\,543\\,032$ is divisible by $3,$ but it is not divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, only I is divisible by $3$ and $9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171757 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b483f9f7-47a9-5725-b1f1-fe0ea39a7e96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 6"}] :question/id #uuid "2d40d35a-54e1-5d01-9e0f-345a290336ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-15013" :question/problem "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $93\\,455\\,13\\square$ divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $3$\n\nII. $6$\n\nIII. $8$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$ Remember that to determine whether a number is divisible by $3,$ we check whether the sum of the digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the given number, the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n9+3+4+5+5+1+3+\\square = 30+\\square.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits we can substitute into the blank.\n\n- If we substitute ${\\color{blue}{3}}$ into the blank, we get $93\\,455\\,13{\\color{blue}{3}},$ which is not divisible by $2.$ Therefore, it is not divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- If we substitute ${\\color{blue}{6}}$ into the blank, we get $93\\,455\\,13{\\color{blue}{6}},$ which is divisible by $2.$ The sum of the digits is $30 + {\\color{blue}{6}} = 36,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\n- If we substitute ${\\color{blue}{8}}$ into the blank, we get $93\\,455\\,13{\\color{blue}{8}},$ which is divisible by $2.$ However, it is not divisible by $3$ because the sum of the digits is $30+{\\color{blue}{8}}=38,$ which is not divisible by $3.$ So, the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171758 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb0ae539-5348-5a2c-b226-c009ce6d6094" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 7"}] :question/id #uuid "dadf214d-16d0-5dbb-aa89-89f4f8e7c79f" :question/math-academy-id "e-15014" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $637$\n\nII. $368$\n\nIII. $112$" :question/worked-solution "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number ${\\color{blue}{63}}{\\color{red}{7}},$ we have that \n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{63}}-2({\\color{red}{7}})=63-14=49\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $637$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number ${\\color{blue}{36}}{\\color{red}{8}},$ we have that \n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{36}}-2({\\color{red}{8}})=36-16=20\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $368$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number ${\\color{blue}{11}}{\\color{red}{2}},$ we have that \n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{11}}-2({\\color{red}{2}})=11-4=7\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $112$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8fa39c-a982-569a-b2e0-833c51259711" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 3 or 9"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17fae707-234b-5507-93c9-8b38a5d9f1bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432707} {:answer/id #uuid "19e13b1c-16f5-5fc8-a671-833b5709b8d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432708} {:answer/id #uuid "af45d2a1-5a3b-5c3e-9120-03abfd5ec846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432743} {:answer/id #uuid "bad2a1ab-31c5-5027-a0be-787091378f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432745} {:answer/id #uuid "d6394eaa-ebbb-50b8-bf10-523ea6eac961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6394eaa-ebbb-50b8-bf10-523ea6eac961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432754} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dcd5f48-4894-5201-9b6d-2e2eb2a453bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9669189-f542-5fc7-9dce-62db6de9555d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132386" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $3?$\n\nI. $935\\,784$\n\nII. $7\\,391\\,123$\n\nIII. $12\\,144\\,801$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $935\\,784$ is\n\n$$\n9+3+5+7+8+4=36,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So, $935\\,784$ is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $7\\,391\\,123$ is\n\n$$\n7+3+9+1+1+2+3=26,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $3.$ So, $7\\,391\\,123$ is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $12\\,144\\,801$ is\n\n$$\n1+2+1+4+4+8+0+1=21,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So,  $12\\,144\\,801$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8fa39c-a982-569a-b2e0-833c51259711" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 3 or 9"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121e7df8-8657-5dcb-a92f-506287be02dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432705} {:answer/id #uuid "6999ccbb-0da9-56ee-9ed1-618bb6718054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432726} {:answer/id #uuid "89c0a663-188b-568b-84c7-12a167670681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432731} {:answer/id #uuid "c423a550-f52a-5b4e-b53b-5d4f5453fe48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218643274